# 26. Authentication + Deep-Link Flow

When an unauthenticated user opens:

```text
/student/projects/123/tasks
```

the intended destination is preserved.

```text
Protected Route
      |
      v
Not authenticated
      |
      v
Role-specific Login
      |
      v
Authentication success
      |
      v
Role resolution
      |
      v
Authorization
      |
      v
Return to intended route
```

Example:

```text
/student/projects/123/tasks
        |
        v
/auth/student/sign-in?returnTo=...
        |
        v
/student/projects/123/tasks
```

The exact query/state transport is an implementation detail; preserving intent is the architectural rule.

