# 110. Navigation Rules to Freeze

## Rule 01
GrowFlow has one unified global top navigation.

## Rule 02
The global top navigation exists across the public website and authenticated application experience.

## Rule 03
The top navigation contains a Workplace control.

## Rule 04
Workplace represents the three GrowFlow role workplaces:
- Student / BUILD
- Mentor / SUPERVISE
- Admin / GOVERN

## Rule 05
Workplace selection is authorization-aware.

## Rule 06
Selecting Student routes to `/student/dashboard`.

## Rule 07
Selecting Mentor routes to `/mentor/overview`.

## Rule 08
Selecting Admin routes to `/admin/overview` only for authorized users.

## Rule 09
Admin is never exposed as a public registration option.

## Rule 10
Logged-out users see separate Login and Sign Up actions.

## Rule 11
Login and Sign Up are not collapsed into one generic CTA.

## Rule 12
Student and Mentor have separate authentication routes.

## Rule 13
Profile lives in the global top navigation.

## Rule 14
Settings is a global authenticated destination.

## Rule 15
Role-specific navigation belongs in the workspace/sidebar layer, not duplicated into the global top bar.

## Rule 16
Global top navigation and role-specific navigation must maintain consistent geometry and interaction behavior.

## Rule 17
Routes are lowercase.

## Rule 18
Multi-word routes use kebab-case.

## Rule 19
Collections use plural resource names.

## Rule 20
Specific resources use IDs.

## Rule 21
Nested routes preserve domain context.

## Rule 22
Project Definition and Student Project Instance remain separate resource hierarchies.

## Rule 23
Major workspace views are route-addressable.

## Rule 24
Short focused actions use modals/drawers.

## Rule 25
Long-running, resumable, or multi-stage operations use workflows.

## Rule 26
Workflow states do not unnecessarily become global routes.

## Rule 27
Deep links are supported.

## Rule 28
Authentication must preserve meaningful intended destinations.

## Rule 29
Authentication is followed by role resolution and authorization.

## Rule 30
Authorization remains backend-authoritative.

## Rule 31
Search is authorization-aware.

## Rule 32
Notifications link to canonical resources.

## Rule 33
Share links use canonical routes.

## Rule 34
Query parameters represent filters/view state; routes represent resource identity.

## Rule 35
Meaningful route navigation survives refresh.

## Rule 36
Browser back navigation works naturally for route-addressable views.

## Rule 37
Project lifecycle state does not create a new navigation tree.

## Rule 38
Long-running AI jobs continue independently of browser/page lifetime.

## Rule 39
AI/RAG/document processing states remain contextual unless independent routing is justified.

## Rule 40
Mobile preserves access to all meaningful navigation destinations.

## Rule 41
The mobile sidebar becomes a navigation drawer.

## Rule 42
Project and group navigation remain contextual on mobile.

## Rule 43
Do not assume multi-role accounts unless explicitly supported by authorization architecture.

## Rule 44
Do not introduce unnecessary standalone routes for transient UI states.

## Rule 45
No Phase 01 surface may disappear without an explicit documented IA decision.

